Tuesday
Today was DCM, definitely fun to see the district once a week. Right before
DCM we had a lesson with Ruriko over the phone, it was good to chat with
her. She read from The Book of Mormon we gave her, but somehow started from
the reference guide first (not sure how but she just had the book backwards
=F0=9F=98=82). Later we had a meal at some member's house, and I was once a=
gain near
perishing. Too much of a good thing is so real. That evening with Tanaka
Kyoudai we taught a lesson about tithing to a young family. It was a loooot
of vocabulary I don't know but I tried my best to be a part of the lesson
lol.

Wednesday
Today we had a lesson with=E2=80=A6 Guzman=E3=81=95=E3=82=93!!! He actually=
 managed to read the
Introduction To The Book of Mormon which we recommended, but he also read
the testimonies of the witnesses as well as the testimony of Joseph Smith
and pretty much taught us a short lesson about it; it was such a positive
spiritual experience, Sonomura=E9=95=B7=E8=80=81 and I were stunned. Will l=
et you know
about how things go next week! I think He's ready ^_^
Today we also had Eikaiwa, which was amazing as usual! Got a =E2=80=9Cknock=
 knock=E2=80=9D
from Toyama=E3=81=95=E3=82=93, we also practiced a conversation Together, m=
essed it up, and
laughed ourselves silly as usual =F0=9F=98=82.

Thursday
Basketball night and Hirakata Eikaiwa, Eikaiwa was over zoom, and we mostly
just talked with Sister Seto and her kids, was pretty funny actually =F0=9F=
=98=82 She
was trying to control them while also paying attention.

Friday
SKK (weekly planning) and YSA gathering, was good preparation as well as
good teaching!

Saturday
This morning we met with Ui=E3=81=8F=E3=82=93 who we haven't seen in like 2=
 months, hrs
been so busy with work. We got Sukiya for breakfast and taught a lesson.
He's still progressing a ton but we gotta just meet with him more. Today we
also met with a dude named Kousei from hellotalk (hellotalk is popping
off). We went to eat sushi together (I was actually the only one that
ordered sushi lol) and we gave him a book of Mormon, said he's definitely
gonna read it, so excited to hear about it! As we were leaving the bike
parking lot, a super tall blonde (and familiar looking, we low key biked
past him a few times before) dude came up to us and just kinda stood there.
Piercing our souls with his gaze. Intense. Anyways we talked to him, and
he's actually an exchange student from Germany, and he's says he's
=E2=80=9Cdetermined to stay in Japan=E2=80=9D and he never wants to go back=
. He shook our
hands and left us with a =E2=80=9CGod bless you=E2=80=9D, which is legitima=
tely unheard of
in Japan bro. He's the chosen one. We bumped into him soon after and got
his contact info, amd he gave me a hug. He is so nice, his name is Paul
=F0=9F=98=81(tears of joy)=F0=9F=98=A2 makes me so happy we met him. Hope t=
o see him soon!
Afterwards we had sports night, Toyama=E3=81=95=E3=82=93 came which was gre=
at! Afterwards
we all ate at Sukiya, which was pretty tasty, but I'm actually not a huge
fan of Sukiya =F0=9F=98=82 I always leave feeling kinda sick.

Sunday
Today we had church as normal, Moriguchi=E3=81=95=E3=82=93 was able to make=
 it today, that
was awesome! We invited her earlier this week, and she said she was busy,
but her kids apparently begged her to take them, so she came after all =F0=
=9F=98=82
Awesome. Most of the rest of the day was spent studying, planning, and
doing media missionary work, not much else to say. There was some pudding
that we were given, and I really did not like it. It was not fish pudding,
but it smelled like cheese, tasted fruity and milky and it was kinda nasty,
not sure why. =F0=9F=98=85 My head hurt a lot throughout today so as I'm wr=
iting this
my brain is definitely foggy, sorry in advance (low key not advance, this
is near the end of the Email =F0=9F=98=82)

P-day/Monday (first =C2=BE) will write the rest next week :)
Today we went to Kyoto again, and went to the place with like 1000 Tori
(Shinto Gates) and took some pictures. We didn't go the whole way because
my feet were low key dying but we still got some solid pictures at least.
Today's been a tough one, there were a few things I had wanted to do and we
didn't get a chance to do any of them, and my feet were killing me the
whole time too =F0=9F=98=B5 It's really frustrating. I'll just wait until n=
ext week
to do something but I could have really used a solid break =F0=9F=98=96

Spiritual thought
I don't feel great right now, but I Am at least confident things will work
out. I believe that all of our lives are the same in a way. I'm sure we all
have sucky moments, but if we look forward with faith it'll never be =E2=80=
=9Ctoo
much=E2=80=9D to bear. Sometimes it's gonna be really heavy and sometimes i=
t'll
feel like it will never pass. But, it will! And it'll be lighter if you
turn outwards, and align yourself with God's will. I'm not doing amazing
with that ATM, I'm gonna try my best! I hope you can too, whoever is
reading this.

Love you all! So much!!
=E3=82=AD=E3=83=AA=E3=82=A2=E3=83=B3=E9=95=B7=E8=80=81

